# WordPress migration cache — holds scraped page HTML and a live session
# cookie for preprod.spenza.com. Never commit this.
.wp-cache/

# macOS-specific files
.DS_Store

# jetbrains setting folder
.idea/

# Mirrored media — served from S3 behind media.spenza.com, not from here.
#
# 11,209 files and 2.2GB. It was committed by the original mirror run, before a
# media host existed, and GitHub rejects a push that large (the pack hits their
# 2GB limit). Nothing needs the bytes: the build drops them from dist/ when
# MEDIA_ORIGIN is set, and the only thing that read them was a filename check,
# which now uses src/data/wp-media-manifest.json instead.
#
# Restore a working copy with `npm run wp:blog-media-sync`, or from the bucket:
#   aws s3 sync s3://spenza-media/wp-content ./public/wp-content
public/wp-content/
public/wp-assets/wp-content/webp-express/
